    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1c797afd_56db7c3e",
        "filename": "driver/usb_mux.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 256,
      "author": {
        "id": 1329040
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-02-14T19:46:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For Intel specific purpose, we are getting the DP mode configuration i.e. A/B/C/D/E/F from amode. Similarly, we are planning to get all the USB mux related information through single host command and we are so getting the cc state info from the usb_pd_protocol.",
      "parentUuid": "c2926419_7747be7c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 256,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 256,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "91072c8a0cb855db7bc8ca74ff946263944f4aa7",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "68be81ca_bb6bccff",
        "filename": "driver/usb_mux.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 256,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-02-14T20:38:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Which states in particular do we care about? Do we care about audio accessory for example?\n\nIf there are only a few of the states that we care about, we can just directly encode them into the flags.\n\n\nThe only other host command that I saw that might fit was ec_response_usb_pd_control and I could see the argument go either either way to put this data in that command instead.",
      "parentUuid": "1c797afd_56db7c3e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 256,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 256,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "91072c8a0cb855db7bc8ca74ff946263944f4aa7",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "27dc7bca_cfe9694e",
        "filename": "driver/usb_mux.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 256,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001696
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-02-14T21:10:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u0027enum pd_cc_states\u0027 doesn\u0027t encode DP alt mode DFP_D pin assignment (rightfully so, I think) so pd_get_cc_state() doesn\u0027t help you at all. Take a look at pd_dfp_dp_get_pin_mode() and how it is used in board usb_pd_policy files instead.\n\nFor a recent non-Intel Chromebook project, we determined we only cared about supporting pin assignment C and E, and we were able to get away with not sharing pin assignment with the host (see https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel/+/chromeos-4.4/drivers/phy/phy-rockchip-typec.c#832) (check with bleung@ to see if it\u0027s still the case). Does only supporting pin assignment C and E make this CL much simpler, or maybe not even necessary at all?",
      "parentUuid": "68be81ca_bb6bccff",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 256,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 256,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "91072c8a0cb855db7bc8ca74ff946263944f4aa7",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5893982e_25859925",
        "filename": "driver/usb_mux.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 256,
      "author": {
        "id": 1296157
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-02-14T21:29:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Following additional configs are needed for Intel MUX configuration than in r-\u003eflags.\n1. role UFP/DP from ec_response_usb_pd_control_v1\n2. DP mode from ec_params_usb_pd_get_mode_response vdo[0] has the info of it\n3. need debug accessory mode info - 1 bit is okay for both Audio \u0026 Debug acc\n4. need cable type (emark/regular) - 1 bit is okay\n\nif we add cc_state we can remove calling ec_response_usb_pd_control_v1 (it will cover 1 \u0026 3)\nDP mode can be clubbed with cc_state (it will cover 2)\ncable type can be added in r-\u003eflags (it will cover 4)",
      "parentUuid": "27dc7bca_cfe9694e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 256,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 256,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "91072c8a0cb855db7bc8ca74ff946263944f4aa7",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1499921f_b8ecfdf9",
        "filename": "include/ec_commands.h",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 4957,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001696
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-02-13T21:23:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You\u0027re proposing to return \u0027enum pd_cc_states\u0027 values here? In that case, you\u0027ll need to move the definition of \u0027enum pd_cc_states\u0027 into this file so users of the host command can decode the value.\n\nBut taking a step back, what is the exact info about the state of the port you need? Can you get that info already from another host command, or encode that info into a new USB_PD_MUX_* flag instead?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4957,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 4957,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "91072c8a0cb855db7bc8ca74ff946263944f4aa7",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e73a414c_408fa922",
        "filename": "include/ec_commands.h",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 4957,
      "author": {
        "id": 1329040
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-02-13T22:24:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I just need the current CC state of the USB_PD mux. I don\u0027t think there is any host command which is giving out this information. I can change it as enum pd_cc_states for the host command to decode the value.",
      "parentUuid": "1499921f_b8ecfdf9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4957,
        "startChar": 1,
